The Open Data Commons Attribution License is a license agreement intended to
allow users to freely share, modify, and use this database while maintaining
this same freedom for others. Many databases are covered by so-called
"database rights" or similar rights, and this license is intended to cover
those rights.

1.0 Definitions
  "Database" means a collection of data arranged in a systematic or methodical
  way.
  "Contents" means the data contained in the Database.
  "Produced Work" means a work created using the Database.

2.0 Rights and obligations
  You are free to Share the Database, to Create a Produced Work from the
  Database, and to use the Database for any purpose, provided that You give
  attribution in the manner specified in the license.

Attribution must be given to the original source of the Database in a manner
reasonable to the medium or means You are utilizing.
